# .egress-allow — third-party network hosts this repo is ALLOWED to contact,
# one per line. See .egress-allow.example for the full rules and the enforce
# switch. This repository is report-only until the list below is complete: the
# application's whole purpose is contacting arbitrary media sites named by the
# person using it, so the hosts worth declaring here are the ones IT chooses,
# not the ones a download reaches.

# The update check in updater.py reads the current yt-dlp release number from
# the package index the dependency is installed from. Request only, no payload,
# at most once a day, and switchable off with check_updates=0 in the settings
# file. Declared because an engine left at the version it happened to resolve
# to on install day is how five CVEs were reported against this repository on
# 2026-09-21.
pypi.org

# The deno check in updater.py reads the vendor's release pointer, one line of
# text, under the same daily throttle and the same check_updates switch. It is
# made only for a deno this account owns (the one `install.sh --with-deno`
# puts in ~/.local/bin); a distribution-packaged deno is shown and never asked
# about, so on those machines this host is never contacted.
dl.deno.land

# Release archives and their published SHA-256 files: `install.sh --with-deno`
# downloads and verifies from here, and `deno upgrade` — run only from the
# Update button — fetches from here as well.
github.com
